      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T21:35:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I noticed this issue when working with banding appearing in blur image filters on phone screens, where the save layer\u0027s restore paint\u0027s dither setting was being ignored. This should mean dithering a large blur result will help avoid banding that appears in its pseudo-gradients.\n\nPS1 -\u003e PS2 shows the bug fixes. PS1 in gold shows the banding on the RHS of the new GM, although only for GPU backends. CPU backend had better checks for dithering and image draws.",
      "revId": "6d10115df8ed9984e728bcaaecbf3a9db95d3ee8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3d0ad08d_ff5f01bf",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-15T01:39:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "although while driving I did realize that this will not be so useful for the blur case since the ideal time to apply the dither would be when upscaling the final blur pass, but at the moment this happens before the restore paint is available. Other optimizations could combine these into the same draw, or we should make dithering something you can specify at each filter stage. Regardless, those would all require the backends to handle dithering on drawImage calls correctly.",
      "parentUuid": "a6c5ea87_ae296c26",
      "revId": "6d10115df8ed9984e728bcaaecbf3a9db95d3ee8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2982017a_b5bf8f2d",
        "filename": "src/core/SkBlitter_Sprite.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 200,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-02-14T21:35:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The new GM doesn\u0027t actually get here because it\u0027s upscaling on the canvas matrix, so doesn\u0027t count as a sprite, but from code inspection, it is theoretically possible that a sprite draw that should otherwise use dithering could get here.\n\nThat being said, visually, maybe dithering at 1-to-1 scale on source colors that have already been packed into a lower bit representation isn\u0027t so meaningful. The improvements are mostly when bilinear filtering to produce new values that have higher precision.\n\nGiven that, should I just drop this check since sprites by definition won\u0027t be changing scale or bilerp? Regular image rect calls on the CPU backend go through the vm blitter or raster pipeline path that correctly handle dithering on the paint.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 200,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 200,
        "endChar": 83
      },
      "revId": "6d10115df8ed9984e728bcaaecbf3a9db95d3ee8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
